1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Meet Havooch, named after an orange cat whose name means carrot.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:09,267
It's a video player that carries your feedback to your coding agent.

3
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:14,600
Pause on any frame, drag a box around what you mean, and write what should change.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,700
Each frame you comment on becomes a numbered thread, and your notes wait in a queue.

5
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:26,500
Then send them all. One batch goes to your agent, with the time, the frame, the region, and the transcript.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:32,533
Your agent knows the project behind the video. It does the work, and makes you a new version.

7
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:38,433
Answers land on the right threads, beside the video. When it's unsure, it asks you there.

8
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:44,133
And there's nothing to set up. No API key, no account, no agents to connect.

9
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:50,333
Havooch talks to the agent you already run. Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and more.

10
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:55,033
Havooch. Watch videos together with your agents.
